[9.397459, "o", "root@5888fae4-a446-4c9f-a3ce-6022c28c8fd7:/app# "]
[15.992333, "i", "nl -ba EXPERIMENT.md\n"]
[15.992529, "o", "nl -ba EXPERIMENT.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[15.994819, "o", "     1\t# EXP-2291 analysis plan (\"related items v2\")\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tWritten and agreed before launch (2026-08-25). The readout must follow this plan. The same plan applies to every\r\n     4\texperiment exported in this layout.\r\n     5\t\r\n     6\t## 1. Question\r\n     7\tDoes variant B (the redesigned related-items module) change click-through on product pages compared with A (the\r\n     8\tcurrent module)?\r\n     9\t\r\n    10\t## 2. Randomization\r\n    11\t- The unit of randomization is the **user**. The assignment service randomizes each user once, 50/50, by a hash of\r\n    12\t  the experiment's salt and the user id, at the user's first eligible product pageview; the user keeps that variant\r\n    13\t  for the whole experiment.\r\n    14\t- `assignments` logs it. The logger retries, so a row can appear more than once, exactly repeated; an exact repeat of\r\n"]
[15.994846, "o", "    15\t  a row counts once. A user never has two different assignment rows.\r\n    16\t\r\n    17\t## 3. Population\r\n    18\t- The experiment is the users the assignment service randomized; a user whose variant was not set by the\r\n    19\t  randomization is not in the experiment.\r\n    20\t- Bot traffic is excluded from both arms, before anything is counted: a user is excluded if the platform's bot\r\n    21\t"]
[15.994864, "o", "  screening flagged the user by a rule that looks only at who the client is (its user agent, network or device),\r\n    22\t  whenever that flag was raised. No user is excluded for anything the user did during the experiment.\r\n    23\t- `n_users` of an arm = the users of the experiment in that arm after the bot exclusion, users with no pageview\r\n"]
[15.995018, "o", "    24\t  included.\r\n    25\t- Only pageviews at or after the user's `assigned_at` count. A pageview with `ts` strictly earlier than `assigned_at`\r\n    26\t  is dropped; one with `ts` equal to `assigned_at` counts.\r\n    27\t- Timestamps are ISO 8601 with a `Z` or a `+hh:mm` / `-hh:mm` offset (both forms occur in the same file). Compare\r\n    28\t  instants, not text.\r\n    29\t\r\n    30\t## 4. Metric\r\n    31\t- A counted pageview is a pageview of a user counted in `n_users`, at or after that user's `assigned_at` (section 3).\r\n    32\t- A counted pageview is clicked when the user opened the page of at least one related product from the module on it;\r\n    33\t  opening two product pages from one pageview is still one clicked pageview.\r\n    34\t- `clicks` of an arm = the number of its clicked counted pageviews; `pageviews` = the number of its counted pageviews.\r\n    35\t- CTR of an arm = clicks / pageviews over the whole arm (a ratio of sums, not the average of per-user CTRs).\r\n    36\t- `diff` = CTR_B - CTR_A (absolute, not re"]
[15.995067, "o", "lative).\r\n    37\t\r\n    38\t## 5. Uncertainty\r\n    39\t- The 95% confidence interval for `diff` must reflect that users, not pageviews, were randomized: the pageviews of one\r\n    40\t  user are not independent of each other. Any one of these is acceptable:\r\n    41\t  - (a) the delta method for each arm's ratio of per-user sums (the sum of the users' clicks over the sum of the\r\n    42\t    users' counted pageviews), treating the arms as independent;\r\n    43\t  - (b) a user-level bootstrap: resample users with replacement within each arm, at least 2,000 resamples, percentile\r\n    44\t    interval;\r\n    45\t  - (c) cluster-robust (CR1) standard errors clustered by user, from a pageview-level regression of the clicked\r\n    46\t    indicator (section 4) on an indicator of B.\r\n    47\t- An interval that treats each pageview as an independent trial is not acceptable.\r\n    48\t\r\n    49\t## 6. Sample ratio mismatch (SRM) check\r\n    50\t- Pearson chi-square goodness-of-fit test of (`n_users` A, `n_users` B) of section 3 against a 50"]
[15.995109, "o", "/50 split: 1 degree\r\n    51\t  of freedom, no continuity correction. `srm_p` is its p-value; `srm_flag` = `srm_p` < 0.001.\r\n    52\t- An SRM means the arms, as counted, are not the groups the randomization made. Find the cause before reading\r\n    53\t  anything else: if the assignment itself is unbalanced, the experiment cannot be read; if a step of the analysis\r\n    54\t  made the imbalance, that step is wrong: fix it and check again.\r\n    55\t\r\n    56\t## 7. Decision rule (apply in this order)\r\n    57\t1. `srm_flag` is true: `\"invalid\"` (the assignment is broken; do not read the result, investigate).\r\n    58\t2. The lower bound of the 95% CI is above 0: `\"ship\"`.\r\n    59\t3. Otherwise: `\"no_ship\"`.\r\n    60\t\r\n    61\t## 8. Input files (one folder per experiment)\r\n    62\tFour gzip-compressed CSV files with a header row: `assignments.csv.gz`, `bot_flags.csv.gz`, `pageviews.csv.gz` and\r\n"]
[15.995148, "o", "    63\t`module_clicks.csv.gz`. Their rows and columns are as the data platform documents them in `docs/DATA_DICTIONARY.md`.\r\n    64\t\r\n    65\t## 9. Output: `result.json`\r\n    66\tA JSON object with at least these keys (more keys are fine):\r\n    67\t\r\n    68\t| Key | Type | Meaning |\r\n    69\t|---|---|---|\r\n    70\t| `n_users` | object `{\"A\": int, \"B\": int}` | section 3 |\r\n    71\t| `pageviews` | object `{\"A\": int, \"B\": int}` | section 4 |\r\n    72"]
[15.995207, "o", "\t| `clicks` | object `{\"A\": int, \"B\": int}` | section 4 |\r\n    73\t| `ctr` | object `{\"A\": number, \"B\": number}` | section 4 |\r\n    74\t| `diff` | number | CTR_B - CTR_A |\r\n    75\t| `ci_95` | array `[lower, upper]` | section 5 |\r\n    76\t| `srm_p` | number | section 6 |\r\n    77\t| `srm_flag` | boolean | section 6 |\r\n    78\t| `decision` | `\"ship\"`, `\"no_ship\"` or `\"invalid\"` | section 7 |\r\n"]
[15.995492, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
